 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm the actions of the Monticello\ncentral school district notwithstanding the failure to timely file final\nbuilding cost reports with the education department",
    "basePrintNo": "S5627",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5627-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5627\n\nSPONSOR: MARTUCCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm the actions of the\nMonticello central school district notwithstanding the failure to timely\nfile final building cost reports with the education department\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide building aid forgiveness to districts that would otherwise\nlose aid due to inadvertent, minor and technical errors.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. states that where the education department denies or has\ndenied building aid or has collected overpayments due and payable prior\nto the 2022-23 school year, such payments shall be legalized.\n\nSection 2. states that the State Education department must inform school\ndistricts with eligible projects by July 1, 2021.\n\nSection 3. defines the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWhen the State or school districts make errors relating to building aid\nthey have to pay the State back money they were provided or become inel-\nigible to lost aid even though the state had budgeted for that expense.\nThese errors tend to be minor in nature, such as a miscommunication\nduring a staff transition or a clerical error. While these errors are\nminor, the amount of money school districts lose out on is not.  Estab-\nlishing a period of forgiveness would encourage legislative efficiencies\nby eliminating the need for standalone bills and also make it easier for\ndistricts to collect their reimbursements. The state has already budget-\ned the aid for districts under these scenarios, so it would not require\nadditional appropriations.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-20: A5768 - referred to Education\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUnknown.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
